Wolf Point wagons using the repaired Bardwell & Otis portable model. Connected waistcoat shoulders, grounded shoes and identity cards distinguish reconstructed appearance and placement from the historically modelled firm.\n\nCanonical authoring/export remains source `96c4da4b` and successful run `39736567239`. The eight Bardwell raw/web GLBs, placement, person data and human runtime are unchanged by the final test repairs and incoming DEV folds. Photographic finishing, complete tailoring, other people/eras, walking, drivers and riders remain open under T-1789.\n\nValidation already observed:\n\n- Authored `248ecfb56`: full preflight 1,048 checks/381 self-tests, committed-HEAD checks and postcommit publication/mirror parity passed.\n- Repaired immutable `248ecfb56`: desktop/mobile stages 1–2 each194/0 and stages9–12 each69/0 passed. Exact census and actual visible glossary meaning/viewport/dismiss assertions remain.\n- Incoming integration `8f5127d4`: supported CI fold and local publication/mirror passed. All four normal workflows passed; the main1048/381 gate, human workflow and moving/upload-release32 actually tested merge `8fc3fd3f0` (DEV7d9 + source8f). Push report tested8f. These are scoped to those actual commits.\n- Original immutablefe98 eighteen-cell batch completed12 PASS/6 FAIL; desktop13 passed160/0. All six obsolete-test failures remain recorded. The repaired cells above replace their affected assertions without relabelling the original batch.\n- Immutable8f: both stage15 and mobile14 passed. Actual8fc merge: mobile14 passed. Both corresponding desktop14 jobs remain pending at the latest observation.\n- Focused published8f mobile passed20/0. Desktop original focused projection timed out after its QA11 assertion passed; a separate six-check projection timed out after the first five release assertions passed. The authentic returning-profile observation separately passed16/0. All timeouts remain failures, with their partial scope preserved; this is not a claim that either timed-out whole projection passed.\n\nCurrent remaining merge work: latest DEV `73aefb020` changes the 1904 Wheeler roof/provenance/feed. Selected supported incoming integration run `39871276267` is active; source remains8f at this update. After its actual push, verify exact parents/tree, run actual new normal CI and fresh published stage14 in both viewports. Existing valid1835/person/UI/15 results retain their source labels; no full-current-head eighteen-cell PASS is claimed.\n\nDEV only. Ordinary merge when the applicable current checks are green. Source, evidence, claims and recovery instructions are periodically committed and pushed to `kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets` (latest checkpoint `bcbf9678`). No broad photographic-parent closure.\n","labels":[{"id":12336280996,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUoK9js8AAAAC30y1pA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/labels/stuck","name":"stuck","description":"No automation in this repo can move this PR — see the comment","color":"B60205","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T22:29:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T00:41:33Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/1835-workwear-repair-20261021","ref":"steward/1835-workwear-repair-20261021","repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","